.TH LUS-LSP 1 "" "Lus" "Lus Manual"
.SH NAME
lus-lsp \- run the language server on standard input and output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBlus lsp\fR [\-\-version]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the language server that is built into \fBlus\fR, which speaks the Language Server Protocol on standard input and output for files with the \fB.lus\fR extension and the language id \fBlus\fR.
An editor or a coding agent starts it as the command \fBlus lsp\fR, so the server always matches the installed version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print the version of the server and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
The client sent shutdown before the end of the input.
.TP
1
The input ended without a shutdown.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lus (1)
.PP
The CLI page of the Lus manual, https://lus.dev/manual/cli#lus-lsp, has the same text with links to the rest of the manual.
